think Lindy-first crux-first: the next durable crux is the feedback delay — the foundational primitive of a whole second wing (echo, chorus, flanger, reverb), exactly as the sidechain opened the keyed wing. Crux = an integer-exact bounded feedback loop that decays and never wraps.
think Key design insight: the delay line is the clip buffer itself (applied in place, left to right), so buf[i-delay] inside the span already holds the output written this pass — true feedback with NO carried state, and split-equals-whole holds for free.
think Self-approved the design round (no custody gate — a new primitive on timeline.saturate), wrote the fill doc, the module, and the witness.
obs First selftest RED on case 4 (EchoDidNotReachSilence): 300 with fb 1/3 over a length-10 clip only reaches 3 on the even lane; shrank the impulse to 30 (30 to 10 to 3 to 1 to 0) so the train reaches silence within the clip. Second run GREEN.
obs Refusal law: fb_num < fb_den is the safety invariant — a feedback at or above unity is a runaway, refused BadFeedback; delay in [1, max_clip]; span within the clip; each before any write.
